# Alfy — copy to .env.local and fill in. The site builds/renders with these blank
# (demo data shows); it goes LIVE once they point at a real Alfy Supabase project.

# ── Frontend (PUBLIC_ = exposed to the browser; safe) ─────────────────────────
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=            # https://<ref>.supabase.co
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=       # anon key (public by design)
PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://askalfy.com

# ── Edge-function secrets — DO NOT put in .env. Set with:
#     supabase secrets set NAME=value --project-ref <ref>
#   SUPABASE_URL
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY             (alfy-connect uses it to identify the caller)
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY     (never ships to the browser)
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY             (platform pays inference — consumers can't BYO over SMS)
#   COMPOSIO_API_KEY              (every outside app — including Google — connects through
#                                  Composio now; see _shared/composio.ts)
#   COMPOSIO_TOOLKITS             (comma-separated, e.g. googlesuper,slack,notion,github —
#                                  Composio stays off until both this and the API key are set)
#   COMPOSIO_AUTHCFG_<TOOLKIT>    (one per toolkit above, uppercased: COMPOSIO_AUTHCFG_GOOGLESUPER,
#                                  COMPOSIO_AUTHCFG_SLACK, ... — the auth config id from Composio)
#   TELNYX_API_KEY                (Mission Control Portal -> Keys & Credentials -> API Keys,
#                                  the v2 key)
#   TELNYX_PHONE_NUMBER           (the provisioned Alfy number, E.164 — +15618137525)
#   TELNYX_PUBLIC_KEY             (Mission Control Portal -> Keys & Credentials -> Public Key
#                                  sub-tab — verifies inbound webhook signatures)
#   SEND_SMS_HOOK_SECRET          (from Auth -> Hooks -> Send SMS once you point it at
#                                  alfy-send-sms-hook's deployed URL — Supabase Auth has no
#                                  built-in Telnyx provider, so phone-login OTPs go through
#                                  this hook instead. Format: v1,whsec_<base64>)
#   INTERNAL_FUNCTION_SECRET      (shared secret for alfy-automation-runner's pg_cron
#                                  caller — there's no human JWT for a scheduled run, so
#                                  cron sends this as x-runner-key instead. Generate any
#                                  long random string; it must match the value baked into
#                                  the cron.schedule(...) call, see docs/alfy-handoff.md)
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY             (Stripe API key — server-side only)
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET         (from the Stripe webhook endpoint you register for
#                                  alfy-stripe-webhook's URL — verifies Stripe-Signature)
#   STRIPE_PRICE_ALFY             (Price id for the "Alfy" $25/mo plan)
#   STRIPE_PRICE_ALFY_PLUS        (Price id for the "Alfy Plus" $75/mo plan — both Products
#                                  + Prices are created once in the Stripe dashboard; can't
#                                  be minted from code without live Stripe credentials)
#
# There is no Google OAuth client to register anymore — Google goes through Composio's
# 'googlesuper' toolkit like every other app, and the connect link is texted to the person
# rather than redirected from the browser. docs/alfy-handoff.md predates that move; treat
# its Google-OAuth steps as history.
#
# src/lib/config.ts's ALFY_PHONE is already set to the provisioned number.
